#  What `gcloud builds submit` uploads for the **judge-replay image only**.
#
#  A second ignore file, and it exists because the two builds want opposite
#  things from one directory. The root `.gcloudignore` describes the context of
#  the *proved* agent and control-plane images, and its last line excludes
#  `packages/muster-ui/` -- correctly, because the frontend is not in either of
#  those containers. The judge-replay image is nothing *but* that frontend, so
#  submitting it under the root file uploads a context without the one
#  directory the Dockerfile needs, and `COPY packages/muster-ui/package.json`
#  fails in build step 0.
#
#  Deleting that line from the root file would fix this build by widening the
#  proved one, which is the wrong direction: the two contexts would drift
#  together and the next thing added for one would arrive in the other. So the
#  judge-replay build names its own file instead, with
#  `--ignore-file=infra/judge-replay.gcloudignore`, and the root file keeps
#  saying exactly what it said before.
#
#  **This one is an allowlist, and that is deliberate.** The image it builds is
#  the only MUSTER artifact meant to be reachable by the public, and a denylist
#  answers the question "is this excluded yet?" -- which is answered wrongly by
#  default every time somebody adds a directory. An allowlist answers "was this
#  named?", so a new directory of fixtures, keys or evidence is out of a public
#  build's context on the day it is created rather than on the day somebody
#  remembers to exclude it.
#
#  Allowlists in this syntax need the ancestors re-included by hand. gcloud
#  prunes an excluded directory rather than descending into it (`FileChooser.
#  GetIncludedFiles`: "Don't bother recursing into skipped directories"), which
#  is `.gitignore`'s rule too -- so `!packages/muster-ui/**` under a `/*` that
#  already dropped `packages/` would match nothing at all. Each level is opened
#  explicitly below, and the last matching pattern wins.
#
#  To see the exact list this produces:
#
#      gcloud meta list-files-for-upload

#  ---- everything, to start with ------------------------------------------
/*

#  ---- the bundle the image builds ----------------------------------------
#
#  The whole UI package: sources, `package.json` and `package-lock.json` for
#  `npm ci`, and the tracked sanitized replay artifacts under `public/cases`
#  that the page reads. Nothing here is a source's private material -- the
#  cases are the same sanitized records the repository serves locally.
!/packages/
/packages/*
!/packages/muster-ui/

#  Local build state, and `node_modules` is a correctness problem rather than a
#  size one: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and only then copies the package in,
#  so an uploaded `node_modules` would overwrite the tree that install just
#  produced with whatever happens to be on the machine that submitted.
/packages/muster-ui/node_modules/
/packages/muster-ui/dist/
/packages/muster-ui/.vite/
/packages/muster-ui/*.local

#  ---- the two files the image is assembled from --------------------------
#
#  The Dockerfile, and the nginx template it copies in. `infra/` is opened only
#  as far as these: the deployment scripts, `env.sh`, the site evidence and
#  `cloudbuild*.yaml` are not part of a static page's context. The build config
#  is not here either, and does not need to be -- `gcloud builds submit
#  --config` reads it locally and sends it as the request's build definition,
#  not out of the uploaded source.
!/infra/
/infra/*
!/infra/docker/
/infra/docker/*
!/infra/docker/judge-replay.Dockerfile
!/infra/docker/judge-replay.nginx.conf.template

#  ---- what is never in this context, said again --------------------------
#
#  Every one of these is already excluded by `/*` above. They are repeated here
#  because an allowlist's absences are invisible, and the point of writing the
#  dangerous ones down is that a future `!` line re-including a parent has to
#  be added *after* an explicit statement that this must not come with it.
#  These are also the patterns the architecture test asserts by name.
/.git/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.specvenv-z3/
/spec/
/docs/
/bench/
/demo/
/artifacts/
/infra/evidence/
/packages/muster-agents/
/packages/muster-kernel/
/packages/muster-platform/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pem
**/*.key
